  "scope": "DOCX passive version-checked bounded package capture and main-view IPC; frontend OPC/document semantics, image decoding/rendering and installed acceptance are separate.",
  "implementation": [
    "New file_delivery_read_docx command uses the existing main-webview caller guard and file_read_check::run. It delegates exact VerifiedFile validation to capture_expected; no path/file URL is returned beyond the existing receipt.",
    "Mechanically extracted the existing XLSX ZIP directory, limits and CRC reader into ooxml_archive.rs. Workbook XML/.rels selection remains unchanged; original workbook_tests.rs is byte-identical. Shared structures and fixed error codes are reused without a new dependency.",
    "DOCX includes XML/.rels plus inert PNG eight-byte signature or JPEG FF D8 FF candidates, regardless of extension. Unsupported binaries remain in entries and are still actually decompressed, counted and CRC checked. No file extraction, linked fetch, external viewer, macro execution or Agent invocation.",
    "Each retained candidate image is at most 8 MiB and there are at most 256. Signatures only select bytes: frontend must validate OPC content types/relations, actual image container/pixels and successful decoding."
  ],
  "contract": {
    "command": "file_delivery_read_docx",
    "input": "{file: VerifiedFile}",
    "success": "{file: VerifiedFile, parts: {name, data(base64)}[], entries: string[], inflatedBytes: number}",
    "failureCodes": [
      "changed",
      "limit",
      "encrypted",
      "unsupported",
      "invalid",
      "unreadable",
      "readPending",
      "readBusy"
    ],
    "formatIdentity": "Backend captures a structurally valid bounded ZIP package; worker must establish DOCX OPC identity and reject active/unsupported relationships. Extension alone is not format proof."
  },
  "limits": {
    "compressedBytes": 16777216,
    "eachPartBytes": 16777216,
    "totalInflatedBytes": 67108864,
    "entries": 2048,
    "candidateImageBytes": 8388608,
    "candidateImages": 256,
    "sharedOsReadSlots": 2,
    "sharedReplyTimeoutSeconds": 15,
    "timeoutQualification": "A timed-out/dropped reply does not abort an OS read or release its slot before the blocking operation actually exits.",
    "memoryQualification": "Logical archive/retained-data budgets; temporary decompression buffers, base64 and IPC clones are not an OS hard heap cap."
  },
